LOCUS       plate7-C10_A_BritishColumbia_PHL-2473_2025_bc1 4772 bp    ds-DNA  circular UNK 02-FEB-2026
DEFINITION  This pHH plasmid contains the HA ectodomain sequence for a H1N1
            variant A/BritishColumbia/PHL-2473/2025. This plasmid was generated
            for the flu-seqneut-2025to2026 library. Signal peptide and 3'NCR
            from WSN, ectodomain from A/BritishColumbia/PHL-2473/2025 HA with
            Genbank accession PX468204_K450R, and last 46 aa recoded WSN
            transmembrane and c-terminal domain. With duplicated 5' packaging
            signals from WSN with a single stop codon in the duplicated
            packaging signal, with the 16-nucleotide barcode CCTAGCCGGAAACATG.
            This plasmid was cloned and sequence confirmed by Twist, and
            designed and logged by Caroline Kikawa.
ACCESSION   .
VERSION     .
KEYWORDS    .
SOURCE      synthetic DNA construct
  ORGANISM  synthetic DNA construct
            .
